    <p class="lede">Your furnace just died. Your AC won’t cool. Your boiler is making noises. The contractor’s on site with a clipboard, and you have to decide: pay $1,800 to fix it, or $9,000 to replace it. This guide explains the financial math, the industry rules of thumb, the regulatory factors (especially R-22 refrigerant), and when the right answer isn’t either option — it’s a heat pump upgrade that does the job of both heating and cooling.</p>
